Building a source package (needed for sbuild, pbuilder, etc.)
===============================================================

This repository has no separate upstream release tarball: `debian/source/format`
is "3.0 (quilt)", which needs one at ../dracon_<upstream-version>.orig.tar.gz.
`dpkg-buildpackage -b` (binary-only, what the top-level instructions use) skips
this and builds straight from the working tree, but anything that goes through
`dpkg-source -b` (sbuild, pbuilder, a plain `dpkg-buildpackage` without -b/-S)
needs the orig tarball to exist first. Generate it from a clean export of the
tree (do not tar up the working directory directly: local build trees such as
build/, .pc/, or anything else untracked will make dpkg-source choke trying to
represent them as part of the source diff):

    version=$(dpkg-parsechangelog -SVersion | sed 's/-[^-]*$//')  # e.g. 1.0
    git archive --format=tar.gz --prefix=dracon-$version/ \
        -o ../dracon_$version.orig.tar.gz HEAD -- . ':!debian'

Uncommitted changes are not picked up by `git archive HEAD`; commit first, or
export from a different treeish (`git stash create`, a temporary commit, ...).

Cross-building for another architecture with sbuild
-----------------------------------------------------

    sbuild --host=arm64 -d stable

sbuild's unshare backend (the default) creates and caches its own "stable"
amd64 chroot on first use under ~/.cache/sbuild/, no manual chroot setup
needed. It builds Architecture: any packages only for a cross build (dracon-
server, dracon-mod-staticcontent, libdracon-dev); python3-certbot-dracon
(Architecture: all) is intentionally skipped - build it once natively instead.

Build-Depends architecture qualifiers matter here: debhelper, cmake, dh-python
and pybuild-plugin-pyproject are all Multi-Arch: foreign and must stay
unqualified (giving debhelper-compat an explicit :native/:<arch> qualifier
makes apt fail to resolve the virtual debhelper-compat (= N) package with
"no choices", even though it resolves fine unqualified). python3-all is
Multi-Arch: allowed, not foreign, and does need the :native qualifier - without
it, apt tries to pull in a target-arch python3 that conflicts with the native
one the build actually runs pybuild/dh_python3 with.
